Solving the (7,5)-Mastermind of Nethack - "You see a drawbridge coming down!"


I just finished a little application to *solve* the Mastermind puzzle at the
Castle's drawbridge with its 7 colors at 5 positions.[*]

For those of you who are as lazy as I am sometimes to solve the Mastermind
puzzle at the Castle's drawbridge, this little program might be of interest.
Check it out if you like at  www.gridbug.de/mm.html  (comments are welcome).


Some details (maybe [OT] for this group, but for those who might want to
know)...

As you see it's a single-line version and yet sufficient for the task, but
it was once intended to become a multi-line version, where you could also
see the history of the previous rounds. Maybe I'll change that at some time
but I don't feel the need, currently (opinions?); so feel free to consider
the current version to be an alpha-release. :-}

At times when I searched the web for any existing algorithm I either found
just strategies described tailored to the original standard (6,4)-Mastermind
or strategies that seemed to me to be suboptimal (I've implemented such a
variant for comparison purposes and you see its performance in Table 2). But
this Mastermind game was so popular that I wouldn't be astonished if there's
anything comparable (or even better) available somewhere; hints appreciated.

Though, the developed algorithm shows very good results (Table 1), as far as
I can judge; with the 4th round it already finds 30% of all 16807 possible
solutions, with the 5th round even 83%, and in the 6th round you have an
excellent 99% probability to have got the right solution, it never needed
more than 8 rounds.

